opening = md`robocoop-5 is restructured so that each thing it tells the model (a tool, a context section, a completion gate, a write report, a loop nudge) is one named cell with a paragraph of prose and a test beside it. Before any code moves, a set of checks is built that fails if the bytes sent to the model change. It is for whoever extends robocoop-5 next: after it, adding a rule is adding a cell, and a refactor is verified without a model run.`
// %%
viewof specStatus = sticky(Inputs.select(["draft", "in review", "approved for handover"], { label: "Status", value: "draft" }), "draft")
// %%
readiness = {
  const notes = (annotations || []).filter((a) => a.home === specModule || (a.anchor && a.anchor.module === specModule));
  const unchecked = requirements.filter((r) => !r.check || /^<.*>$/.test(r.check.trim()));
  const blocking = questions.filter((q) => q.blocking && !q.answer);
  const undrawn = states.filter((s) => !s.drawing);
  const items = [
    [notes.length, "annotations to resolve"],
    [blocking.length, "blocking questions open"],
    [unchecked.length, `of ${requirements.length} requirements without a check`],
    [undrawn.length, `of ${states.length} states without a drawing`]
  ];
  const ready = items.every(([n]) => n === 0) && specStatus === "approved for handover";
  return htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:1.2em;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;font:13px system-ui;padding:.5em .8em;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);border-radius:6px">
    <strong>${ready ? "Ready to hand over" : "Not ready to hand over"}</strong>
    ${items.map(([n, label]) => htl.html`<span style=${{ opacity: n ? 1 : 0.5 }}><strong>${n}</strong> ${label}</span>`)}
  </div>`;
}
// %%
md`## Reviewing this spec

- **Leave a note**: ☰ → Annotate → Note, then drag over the words or click the shape. Notes are review comments; Claude Code works through them, and you delete each when it is dealt with.
- **Ask about a spot**: ☰ → Annotate → Ask, then pick the words or shape and type. The question goes to the agent with what you pointed at, and the answer threads at that spot.
- **Click prose** to rewrite it.
- **Ask** in the pane at the bottom. Roboco-op reads and edits this notebook.
- ☰ → **Save in place** keeps your edits and notes in this file.

What needs your eye first: the **rule inventory** (is each row a real rule, and is the fires / silent case the right one), the **Words** (the vocabulary the refactored notebook will use), the **Decisions** table, and the four open questions.`
// %%
md`## Problem

Measured 2026-10-04 with \`tools/code-metrics-cli.ts\` on the working copies of the seven modules (all reported \`clean\` by \`lope-sync.ts status\`; canonical is \`lopebooks/notebooks/@tomlarkworthy_robocoop-5.html\`): 165 cells, 7,136 lines. 26 cells over 40 lines hold 79% of the code.`
// %%
moduleMetrics = [
  { module: "robocoop-5-srctools", cells: 18, loc: 3364, big: 9, pctInBig: 96, md: 1, tests: 0 },
  { module: "robocoop-5", cells: 26, loc: 972, big: 2, pctInBig: 76, md: 1, tests: 3 },
  { module: "robocoop-5-core", cells: 19, loc: 751, big: 3, pctInBig: 77, md: 9, tests: 0 },
  { module: "robocoop-5-engine", cells: 29, loc: 629, big: 3, pctInBig: 67, md: 0, tests: 0 },
  { module: "robocoop-5-sessions", cells: 36, loc: 607, big: 4, pctInBig: 46, md: 1, tests: 6 },
  { module: "robocoop-5-tools", cells: 23, loc: 451, big: 2, pctInBig: 48, md: 1, tests: 0 },
  { module: "robocoop-5-context", cells: 14, loc: 362, big: 3, pctInBig: 40, md: 1, tests: 0 }
]
// %%
moduleMetricsTable = Inputs.table(moduleMetrics, {
  header: { module: "module", cells: "cells", loc: "lines", big: "cells > 40 lines", pctInBig: "% of lines in those", md: "md cells", tests: "test cells" },
  rows: 8
})
// %%
md`Largest cells: \`applyLib\` 871 lines (cyclomatic complexity 497), \`valueTools\` 761, \`fileTools\` 749, \`robocoop5\` 678, \`createAgentSession\` 356, \`specLib\` 260, \`systemPrompt\` 215.

Three things follow from that shape.

**A rule cannot be pointed at.** robocoop-5 was trained run by run (\`knowledge/training-robocoop-5.md\`); each fix added a check that reports something to the model. The source cites 78 run ids or dates in comments (core 6, engine 11, sessions 5, srctools 56). The inventory below lists ${rules.length} such rules. They are closures inside the large cells, so none has a name another cell can import, a paragraph of prose, or a test. ${rules.filter(r => /^yes/.test(r.covered)).length} of ${rules.length} are exercised by any check that runs without a model.

**One pattern has five implementations.** "An ordered list of named checks, each returning a string or null, concatenated for the model" is written separately as: context providers (\`rc5-context\` registry), monitors (\`rc5-monitors\` registry), completion gates (a \`??\` chain inside \`makeSession\`), write feedback (sequential string appends inside \`applyModuleSrc\`), and loop nudges (inline in \`createAgentSession\`). Two are registries; three are hard-coded.

**Three singletons are shared by every session on the page.** Read from the code on 2026-10-04, not reproduced: \`rc5_monitorBus\` is one object drained by each session, so a monitor line goes to whichever session steps first; \`rc5_specGate\` holds one page-wide scorecard, so a failing spec in one session vetoes completion in another; \`watchTable\` renders the legacy \`rc5_watchBus\` only, not a session's own bus. Multi-session shipped 2026-09-27 (\`plan/robocoop-5-multi-session.md\`).

The existing checks do not cover a refactor. \`tools/robocoop-5/\` holds 14 scripts; the ones that assert on rule behaviour are \`guard-unit-test.mjs\` (the once-per-turn completion guard), \`context-unit-test.mjs\` (21 assertions on \`composeContext\`), \`write-feedback-check.mjs\` (values and downstream recompute in an apply message), \`spec-lock-check.mjs\` and \`tests/robocoop5/speclock.test.mjs\`. The notebook holds 9 \`test_*\` cells, all in \`robocoop-5\` and \`robocoop-5-sessions\`. The 113 rc5-train evals with an \`oracle\` score task outcomes, not the text a rule returns.`
// %%
md`## Outcome

- A command prints one hash for everything the model is sent on a fixed scripted session (system prompt, tool schemas, context block, notices, tool results, gate rejections). The hash is the same before the refactor and after every commit that claims to be a pure move.
- Every row of the rule inventory has \`covered: yes\`, naming a test cell that fails when that rule's check is replaced with \`() => null\`.
- A new completion gate, write reporter, monitor, context section or tool is added by defining one cell and registering it. No existing cell is edited.
- No cell in the seven modules is longer than 150 lines, except \`createAgentSession\` and \`createOpenRouterClient\`, which are single state machines and stay whole.
- Two sessions open on one page do not see each other's monitor lines, spec scorecard or watches.`
// %%
md`### Size

Estimated, not measured: three days for the safety net (steps 1 to 4), six days for the moves (steps 5 to 12), one day for the three behaviour fixes (step 13). If time runs out, cut from the bottom of the Steps list. The safety net is not cut: it is useful with no refactor at all.`
// %%
md`## Scope

### Not your concern, do not build it

- **\`@tomlarkworthy/runtime-sdk\`**: nothing is added to it. Helpers that read the runtime for robocoop-5's purposes stay in robocoop-5.
- **Storage keys**: \`robocoop4_model\`, \`robocoop5_speclock\`, \`robocoop5_reasoning_off\`, \`robocoop5_temperature\` keep their names. No migration.
- **\`@tomlarkworthy/robocoop-5-sessions\`** session log format (\`@<group>/<id>\` modules, turn cells): unchanged.
- **The eval harness** (\`tools/robocoop-5/eval/\`, \`tools/robocoop-eval/\`): used as it is. \`driver-core.mjs\` reads \`toolsView\` by name; that name stays.
- **The pairing channel and the Claude runner** (\`lopecode-plugin\`): unchanged.
- **switchboard, annotate, lopepage-2**: they call \`robocoop5(opts)\` and \`rc5Thread\`; those signatures stay.
- **The markdown wiki** and its \`wiki_triggers\`: content unchanged.
- **Prompt wording**: no instruction text is improved, shortened or corrected here, including text that is known to be wrong (listed under Known traps). Wording changes need a model run and are a separate piece of work.

### Non-goals

- Raising a benchmark score. The measure of this work is that scores cannot have moved, because the bytes did not.
- Converting the training evals to rule tests. They test outcomes with a model; rule tests test one check with none.
- A generic agent framework. The registries serve robocoop-5's five rule kinds and nothing else.`
// %%
md`## Words

The refactored notebook uses this vocabulary in cell names and prose. Each term is one thing; the implementer does not introduce synonyms.`
// %%
copy_title = md`Roboco-op 5: an agent that edits the notebook it lives in`
// %%
copy_opening = md`Roboco-op 5 is a chat agent inside a lopecode notebook. It reads and writes the notebook's modules as files, runs them in the live runtime, and is told after each step what its changes did. Everything it tells the model is a cell in one of these modules: a **tool**, a **context section**, a **rule**. Each rule records the run that made it necessary.`
// %%
copy_strings = md`| term | meaning | cell name prefix |
|---|---|---|
| rule | a named check \`{id, kind, check, evidence}\`; \`check\` returns a string for the model or null | \`rule_\` |
| gate | a rule run when the model calls \`task_complete\`; a string refuses the completion | \`rule_gate_\` |
| reporter | a rule run after a module write; its string is appended to the write's result | \`rule_report_\` |
| refusal | a rule run before a write; a string stops the write | \`rule_refuse_\` |
| nudge | a rule run by the loop when a model reply cannot be acted on | \`rule_nudge_\` |
| monitor | a rule run once per step; its string is a notice | \`rule_monitor_\` |
| context section | a provider \`{id, scope, priority, render}\` composed into the context block | \`ctx_\` |
| tool | \`defineTool({id, description, parameters, execute})\` | \`tool_\` |
| evidence | the run id or date and one sentence of what happened, as data on the rule | |
| wire | every byte sent to the model: system prompt, tool schemas, messages | |
| pure move | a commit after which the wire hash is unchanged | |`
// %%
md`## Rule inventory

Read from the source 2026-10-04. One row per check that puts text in front of the model. \`run\` is the run id or date cited in the comment beside the rule; a dash means the source cites none. \`fires\` and \`silent\` are the two test cases to write. \`covered\` names an existing check that would fail if the rule were removed, or \`no\`.

Counted by kind and coverage: ${Object.entries(rules.reduce((a, r) => (a[r.kind] = (a[r.kind] || 0) + 1, a), {})).map(([k, n]) => `${n} ${k}`).join(", ")}; ${rules.filter(r => /^yes/.test(r.covered)).length} covered, ${rules.filter(r => /^partial/.test(r.covered)).length} partly, ${rules.filter(r => r.covered === "no").length} not.`
// %%
rules = [
  { id: "loop-principles", kind: "prompt", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "-", fires: "any session: LOOP_PRINCIPLES is appended to the system prompt", silent: "not applicable", covered: "no" },
  { id: "stall", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "-", fires: "reply is text with no tool call, completion protocol on, fewer than stallNudgeLimit stalls", silent: "reply carries a tool call", covered: "no" },
  { id: "length", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "-", fires: "finish_reason length and no tool call", silent: "finish_reason stop gets the stall text instead", covered: "no" },
  { id: "restated-reply", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "rc5-train m8", fires: "after a nudge, a reply of 400+ chars restates the previous one: turn ends", silent: "second reply differs or is under 400 chars", covered: "no" },
  { id: "malformed-call", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "-", fires: "empty message with finish_reason error or MALFORMED_FUNCTION_CALL", silent: "empty message with finish_reason stop", covered: "no" },
  { id: "truncated-args", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "-", fires: "tool call arguments are JSON cut mid-string", silent: "arguments parse", covered: "no" },
  { id: "batched-completion", kind: "gate", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "20260929-0620-m58-before", fires: "task_complete sent in the same step as another tool call: NOT ended", silent: "task_complete alone", covered: "no" },
  { id: "guard-once-per-turn", kind: "gate", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "-", fires: "completeGuard returns a string on the first completion: REJECTED", silent: "second completion in the turn is accepted", covered: "yes: tools/robocoop-5/guard-unit-test.mjs" },
  { id: "unknown-tool", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "tau-airline arm", fires: "call names a tool the session does not have", silent: "call names a registered tool", covered: "no" },
  { id: "text-only-model", kind: "nudge", module: "core", cell: "createAgentSession", run: "20260929-0620-m74", fires: "client error matches 'support image input' and the history holds an image", silent: "any other client error", covered: "no" },
  { id: "output-truncated", kind: "reporter", module: "core", cell: "truncate", run: "-", fires: "tool output longer than toolOutputLimit", silent: "output under the limit", covered: "no" },
  { id: "zero-tool-calls", kind: "gate", module: "core", cell: "zeroToolCallGate", run: "tau-airline B5", fires: "completion in a turn with no tool call and a summary that does not address the user", silent: "one tool call this turn, or the summary addresses the user", covered: "no" },
  { id: "spec-failing", kind: "gate", module: "tools", cell: "specGateCheck", run: "-", fires: "scorecard has failing examples and the summary has no SPEC-WAIVER: marker", silent: "green scorecard, null scorecard, or waiver", covered: "yes: tests/robocoop5/speclock.test.mjs" },
  { id: "unwritten", kind: "gate", module: "engine", cell: "makeSession", run: "20260928-0847-w9", fires: "a module write was refused or failed and no later write to that path landed", silent: "a later write to the same path landed", covered: "no" },
  { id: "untried-controls", kind: "gate", module: "engine", cell: "makeSession", run: "20260929-0620-m69", fires: "a module with viewof cells was written this turn and try_control was not called since", silent: "try_control used the module, or the session has no try_control tool", covered: "no" },
  { id: "tools-changed", kind: "monitor", module: "engine", cell: "makeSession", run: "20260929-0620-m44", fires: "a tool id was added or removed since the previous step", silent: "first step (baseline), or no change", covered: "no" },
  { id: "watch-updates", kind: "monitor", module: "tools", cell: "createWatchBus", run: "-", fires: "a watched cell recomputed to a new value since the last drain", silent: "same value, or nothing watched", covered: "no" },
  { id: "spec-notice", kind: "monitor", module: "srctools", cell: "specMonitor", run: "-", fires: "@user/spec has failing examples", silent: "no @user/spec module, or all pass", covered: "partial: tools/robocoop-5/spec-lock-check.mjs (browser)" },
  { id: "self-edit", kind: "refusal", module: "sessions", cell: "guardTools", run: "-", fires: "write_file, edit_file or attach_file targets @tomlarkworthy/robocoop-5-* (not the UI module) or a session module", silent: "target is a user module", covered: "yes: test_guardTools" },
  { id: "wiki-unread", kind: "refusal", module: "srctools", cell: "fileTools", run: "rc5-train m28", fires: "written text adds a construct matching a wiki doc's trigger and the session has not read that doc", silent: "doc was read, or the construct was already in the module", covered: "no" },
  { id: "would-delete-cells", kind: "refusal", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "pairing 2026-09-28", fires: "write drops cells that were added after the agent last read the file", silent: "dropped cells were in the last read", covered: "no" },
  { id: "no-default-export", kind: "refusal", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "-", fires: "module source has no export default define", silent: "source has one", covered: "no" },
  { id: "compile-failed", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "-", fires: "source does not parse: FAILED TO COMPILE with line:col", silent: "source parses", covered: "no" },
  { id: "erroring-cells", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m30", fires: "a written cell rejects: ERRORING at runtime, FIX before task_complete", silent: "all cells compute: the all-compute line", covered: "partial: tools/robocoop-5/write-feedback-check.mjs" },
  { id: "failed-test-is-finding", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m1", fires: "the erroring cell is named test_*", silent: "erroring cell is not a test", covered: "no" },
  { id: "pending-cells", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "-", fires: "a cell has no value after 2 s", silent: "cell settles within 2 s", covered: "no" },
  { id: "stale-variable", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m34", fires: "a read meets the runtime's variable_stale sentinel", silent: "value is current", covered: "no" },
  { id: "anonymous-cell-error", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m14", fires: "an unnamed cell rejects", silent: "unnamed cells compute", covered: "no" },
  { id: "markup-as-text", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0040-w9", fires: "an element's text contains markup or an SVG node is in the wrong namespace", silent: "markup rendered as elements", covered: "no" },
  { id: "object-in-text", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-w14", fires: "displayed text contains [object ...]", silent: "no such text", covered: "no" },
  { id: "invalid-svg-attr", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0235-w17", fires: "an SVG attribute holds an invalid value", silent: "attributes valid", covered: "no" },
  { id: "placeholder-in-text", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m35", fires: "displayed text contains NaN, undefined or Infinity", silent: "no such text", covered: "no" },
  { id: "empty-chart", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0610-w31", fires: "a plot or svg draws no marks, or a flat area path", silent: "chart has marks", covered: "no" },
  { id: "arity", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-w17", fires: "a cell function has more parameters than its $def lists inputs", silent: "counts match", covered: "no" },
  { id: "binding-by-position", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m16", fires: "a parameter name differs from the input bound at its position (including viewof_ / mutable_ forms)", silent: "names line up", covered: "no" },
  { id: "orphan-function", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "rc5-train m16", fires: "a const _x = function is declared and no $def uses it", silent: "every function has a $def", covered: "no" },
  { id: "def-without-function", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "rc5-train m20", fires: "a $def names a function the file does not declare", silent: "all declared", covered: "no" },
  { id: "bare-control", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "rc5-train w32", fires: "a cell returns an input element and is not a viewof", silent: "control is a viewof cell", covered: "no" },
  { id: "table-not-editable", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "rc5-train w11", fires: "Inputs.table is passed an editable option", silent: "no such option", covered: "no" },
  { id: "downstream", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "-", fires: "a written cell has dependents in other modules: lists up to 12", silent: "no dependents", covered: "yes: tools/robocoop-5/write-feedback-check.mjs" },
  { id: "structure", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "rc5-train m16", fires: "a cell's maintainability index is under 65 and it is not a literal", silent: "index 65 or over, or a literal cell", covered: "no" },
  { id: "values-changed", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m2", fires: "cells the write did not touch now show different values", silent: "values unchanged: the unchanged line", covered: "partial: tools/robocoop-5/write-feedback-check.mjs" },
  { id: "removed-cells", kind: "reporter", module: "srctools", cell: "applyLib", run: "20260928-0847-m20", fires: "the write removed a test or display cell", silent: "nothing removed", covered: "no" },
